# Fix Groq API Errors (Key Rotation & Token Limits)

This plan addresses the two root causes of the AI failures: the hardcoded `max_tokens` exceeding free tier limits, and the flawed API key rotation logic that always fails on the first key.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Fix Backend AI Client (`backend/ai/llm_client.py`)
Currently, this file has `max_tokens=1500` (which breaks the 1000 limit) and uses the flawed `get_groq_client()` logic.
- Remove the local `get_groq_client` loop.
- Introduce a robust wrapper function `execute_with_fallback()` that takes the completion arguments.
- The wrapper will loop through all 11 API keys. It will attempt the API call, and if it catches a `RateLimitError` (429) or authentication error, it will immediately retry with the next key in the list.
- Decrease `max_tokens` from 1500 to 800 to fit safely within the free tier.

